  "final": "The one-cent errors came from `line_total_cents` in `billing/totals.py`. I fixed it, and the 6 existing tests pass. I didn't add a test for the half-cent cases.\n\n**Cause:** the function did its math in binary floats and then rounded with Python's `round()`. Floats can't represent many decimal prices exactly, so a value that should be a half-cent can land just below it. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even number. The README says amounts round half up, so some rows came out one cent low.\n\n**Fix:** the function now uses `Decimal` arithmetic and rounds with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The invoice `TOTAL` was already a sum of these per-line cent values, so it is corrected too.\n\nI spot-checked three half-cent cases with the new code. 1.005 now gives 101 cents, 2.675 gives 268, and 0.70 × 3 at 5% tax gives 221. I didn't run your real CSV, so any totals you've already sent out will need regenerating.",
